{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I stood between HaShem and you.</b> The sage R. Abraham, of blessed memory, explained: after the standing at Mount Sinai. And the correct interpretation is what the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote — that he is speaking at the time of the giving of the Torah, for Moses would speak and translate to Israel what Elohim would answer him in a voice. And since all Israel heard the first two commandments and understood them from the mouth of the Almighty, but the rest of the commandments they heard from the mouth of the Almighty yet did not understand them from His mouth, therefore Moses needed to translate and explain to Israel so that they would understand. And this is what he said: 'I stood between HaShem and you, to tell you the word of HaShem' — that is, what you did not understand from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He — 'because you feared the fire and did not ascend the mountain, unlike me,' as it is said (Exodus 20:18): ״ומשה נגש אל הערפל״." "<b>To say.</b> When he would say the Ten Commandments to you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:50.547312332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}